 *     stored (name, short description tagline, author, icon, download
 *     count, canonical umod.org URL). NO per-plugin JSON is ever fetched.
 *   - No plugin .cs source file is ever downloaded/mirrored — `download_url`
 *     is stored as a link only, resolved by the worker at install time,
 *     exactly like every other source's importer in this repo.
 *   - There is in fact no richer "body" text to fetch even if ToS were
 *     clear: the per-plugin JSON (`/plugins/<slug>.json`) was checked live
 *     and carries the SAME short `description` field as the listing, no
 *     separate long-form field the way Modrinth has `body` — so this
 *     script cannot and does not claim to fix NxLabs's description-length
 *     problem for uMod the way the Modrinth/Steam/Thunderstore fixes do.
